firmation naming the app. Confirming removes the app through the shared app library and closes the menu. Cancelling closes the dialog and returns focus without removing anything. Non-app rows ignore the key."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN"],"title":"When the rows do not fit, the list height ends mid-row: the clipped peek row tells the eye there is more below the fold. The height never lands exactly on a row boundary, and the card never exceeds 70 percent of panel height."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-C8HX","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5"],"title":"finishRequest with a null selection (Escape/cancel) creates only the done file, so the caller observes the cancel as an empty selection."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-CYB9","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ"],"title":"Absent an exact id, a route equal to a declared alias resolves to the id of the item declaring the alias. Alias comparison lowercases and maps underscores to dashes."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-P708"],"title":"Drilling in pushes the previous menu on the navigation stack. Backspace/Left pops it, or falls back to the parent menu when the stack is empty. Entering a menu clears the filter."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-DQ9P","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6"],"title":"A row matches only when every query term appears in its name text (label, leaf id, aliases) or as a whole word in its description. Invisible and disabled rows never match."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["input_domain"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW"],"title":"The parser strips full-line // comments and trailing commas before JSON parsing, so the authored JSONC parses to its declared entries."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-EFNR","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A"],"title":"swapProviderRows drops exactly the rows carrying the re-run provider's providerMenu and appends the new batch, leaving static children and other providers' rows untouched."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-FGZQ","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5"],"title":"finishRequest with a selection writes the value to the selection file and creates the done file, shell-quoted, and only then closes."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-JRW1","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-47T8"],"title":"Applied guard results drive the view. A row hides when its when: is false. A static submenu or link hides when no descendant is visible, while provider-backed menus stay visible. A checked:true or disabled:true row earns the check-mark label. A disabled row dims and skips the cursor."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-N3RM","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","SYS-REQ-260927-WC89"],"title":"When a route resolves to an action item with a non-empty action, the action runs directly and no menu opens."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-NM45","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-P708"],"title":"A dmenu option may lead with a glyph TAB and trail a subtext TAB. The picker shows the glyph but never returns it. A subtext-bearing pick returns 'label TAB subtext' as the stable key."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-PRNV","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ"],"title":"An exact id match wins over every alias. App rows are never routable, so an installed app's keywords cannot shadow a menu route (htop ships Keywords=system)."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6"],"title":"Scores tier exact label, whole-word app name, label prefix, label substring, name text, then description. Menus and links promote by 2, apps demote by 5 within a tier. Final order breaks ties by depth then declaration order."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6"],"title":"Search lists current-menu matches before deeper (drilldown) matches, with a divider section exactly when both groups are non-empty."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-XW52","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ"],"title":"When a route resolves to a link item, the menu opens at the link's target."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z48F","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["boundary"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-P708"],"title":"Cursor movement lands on the next selectable row in the direction of travel, wrapping at the list ends. Movement steps over disabled rows."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z680","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["atomicity"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A"],"title":"mergeAppRows and swapProviderRows return fresh maps that drop orphan ids and the replaced batch. They list a duplicated incoming id once and never write into their input maps."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260928-8VJQ","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["path_pair_agreement"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ"],"title":"A menu action may exactly match the bare-summon grammar: omarchy-shell shell summon <id>, plus an optional single-quoted payload. The payload carries no embedded quote and the id draws from [A-Za-z0-9._-]+. Such an action executes in-process via shell.summon(id, payload) instead of spawning bash. An absent payload defaults to an empty object literal, matching the bin/omarchy-shell argv default exactly. Any action outside that grammar falls back to the unchanged execDetached bash path. The fast path must preserve semantics: same plugin id, same payload bytes, same default."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260929-B8N9","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["malformed_input"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW"],"title":"The merged item tree is addressable by id. An id present in the tree yields its item, and any other id yields null. Menu state then falls back to the root menu instead of a dangling entry."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260929-DXFJ","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["edge_case"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN"],"title":"After the first filter keystroke or submenu move, the card top edge and the maximum rows height freeze at their current values. The card then grows and shrinks downward instead of re-centering on every resize. Closing the menu clears the freeze, so the next open centers again."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260929-T378","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["edge_case"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-P708"],"title":"Row selection follows the pointer only after it genuinely moves past the gate threshold. It never lands on a non-selectable row. Keyboard navigation, filtering, menu transitions, the delete dialog, and opening the menu disarm the gate. Synthetic hover churn under a stationary pointer therefore cannot move the selection."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["atomicity"],"parent":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"],"title":"Dynamic rows (apps, provider enumerations) replace their source's previous batch atomically: orphans dropped, duplicates listed once, static rows untouched."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["boundary"],"parent":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"],"title":"Activating a row runs its action, follows its link, or drills into its submenu. The cursor never rests on a disabled row. Back navigation retraces the drill path."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["boundary","error_handling"],"parent":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"],"title":"The default JSONC and the user extension merge into one ordered item tree: per-key user overrides, stable order, inferred kinds and parents, injected root."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["boundary"],"parent":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"],"title":"A route string (exact id, declared alias, or normalized spelling) opens the item it denotes; unknown strings fall through as literal ids."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6","matchLevel":"file","parent":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"],"title":"A filter query narrows to visible, selectable rows whose name or description matches every term, ranked by match quality."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260927-WC89","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["error_handling"],"relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260912-XJ5D"],"title":"The menu Lock row invokes the lock component's CLI entry point omarchy-system-lock with no arguments. The callee engages the session lock and exits 0. This is the only menu-to-lock interaction; lock never calls menu."}],"total":36},"readiness":"not_assessed","requiredAuthority":{"acceptedIdentitySources":["github_login","portal_user"],"basis":"approved_policy","enforcement":"portal_or_forge","policyDigest":"sha256:bc649c7377f819faae0f5f9526d0e5c06880645d5c0fab402effd0ac611da76e","policyRevision":"58cd8018b7ae7d6f96900e95c98b7d2fae3aacd0","role":"reviewer"},"routineEvidence":{"claimsObservedPass":38,"gatesAdvisory":27,"gatesNotApplicable":1,"gatesPassed":178,"testsPassed":12},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.decision-summary.v1","scope":{"approximations":["Function-level mapping comes from trace targets `path:symbol` / line ranges (authored + derived) and function-local annotations; a whole-file trace is file-level (weak) and says nothing about which function a requirement needs.","Intent relations: requirement level = satisfies/parent or siblings under a parent with <= 20 children; component level = shared component (incl. traces.components); contract level = an interface requirement naming both components. A missing spec edge can make a real dependency look uncodified, and a broad contract can make an uncodified dependency look related — every candidate is a question for a reviewer, not a verdict on the code or the spec.","Removed-code traces: targets naming a removed/renamed/moved function or a deleted file, and requirement ids cited on removed diff lines that the evaluated file no longer cites. remainingTraces counts the requirement's other code targets at the evaluated revision without re-checking that each still resolves.","Renamed/moved detection is best effort: a removed and an added function with the same name in different files are \"moved\"; a different name with >= 80% identical normaliz